SYSTEM: Maritime message relay (remote maritime communications) - A vessel holds a queue of outbound messages and can forward them to shore over two links.
ACTIONS:
{"description":"Forward messages from the vessel queue over a chosen link.","name":"send","params":[{"choices":["buoy","sat"],"description":"Link to use: solar buoy relay or satellite uplink.","name":"via","type":"enum"},{"description":"How many messages to forward.","max":3.0,"min":1.0,"name":"n","type":"int"}]}
{"description":"Ask the vessel's message handler to prioritize.","name":"prioritize","params":[]}
{"description":"Do nothing this step.","name":"wait","params":[]}
OBSERVED FIELDS:
{"description":"Step counter.","name":"t","type":"int"}
{"description":"Messages waiting on the vessel.","name":"queue","type":"int"}
{"description":"Priority messages waiting on the vessel.","name":"priority_waiting","type":"int"}
